WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:03.909
There's no supervillain quite like Thanos,
the Mad Titan.

00:00:03.909 --> 00:00:07.960
He's been a menace to the Marvel Universe
since 1973, when he made his debut in Iron

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.680
Man #55 — and few villains have proven as
formidable.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.460
Despite his long history in Marvel Comics,
Thanos has never been as high-profile as he

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.460
is now.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.940
You probably already know that he's a nihilistic
cosmic warlord who's set on assembling the

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:23.289
Infinity Gauntlet, allowing him to wipe out
life as we know it.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.581
Set that aside, though, and you'll find a
ton of fascinating components to the character

00:00:26.581 --> 00:00:28.519
that are slightly lesser known.

00:00:28.519 --> 00:00:30.550
This is the untold truth of Thanos.

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:32.510
"Tell me his name again."

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.710
Aesthetic inspiration

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.360
Thanos is far from the most unique creation
in the history of comics.

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:42.370
Created by writer and artist Jim Starlin,
Thanos shares many similarities with characters

00:00:42.370 --> 00:00:47.280
created by another comics luminary, Jack Kirby
— specifically Kirby's work on DC's New

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.590
Gods series.

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:52.840
Starlin initially based Thanos on the New
Gods character Metron, a genius celestial

00:00:52.840 --> 00:00:55.290
observer to the events of the DC universe.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:59.449
Many have thought Thanos' inspiration to be
the DC character Darkseid, but according to

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:01.739
Starlin, that wasn't initially the case.

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:05.199
Speaking in a 1998 interview with Comic Book
Artist, Starlin said,

00:01:05.199 --> 00:01:08.590
"You’d think that Thanos was inspired by
Darkseid, but that was not the case when I

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:09.590
showed up.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:12.659
In my first Thanos drawings, if he looked
like anybody, it was Metron.

00:01:12.659 --> 00:01:15.850
[...] Roy took one look at the guy in the
Metron-like chair and said: 'Beef him up!

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.990
If you’re going to steal one of the New
Gods, at least rip off Darkseid, the really

00:01:18.990 --> 00:01:19.990
good one!'"

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.270
Fortunately, the resemblance is only skin
deep.

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:26.799
The two characters have vastly different motivations
and levels of empathy, and Thanos has fleetingly

00:01:26.799 --> 00:01:28.619
fought alongside heroes before.

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:31.259
We think it's safe to say that's not really
Darkseid's style.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:33.480
"I grant you a quick death."

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:39.590
My name is...

00:01:39.590 --> 00:01:43.470
This may come as a shock from the looks of
him, but Thanos descends from a race of aliens

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.810
that actually look more or less human.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.160
Thanos is a carrier of the Deviant gene, sort
of the equivalent of a mutant in his race.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.060
His mother, father, and the rest of his family
are members of a superpowered alien race called

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:57.070
the Eternals, living on Titan, one of Saturn's
moons.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:00.909
They look human, and when his mother Sui-San
became pregnant, they expected him to look

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:01.909
the same.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:05.390
When Thanos was born, however, one look at
him sent all expectations went out the window

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.019
— including the name his mother intended
to give him.

00:02:08.019 --> 00:02:12.090
Before she realized Thanos was a Deviant,
his mother intended to name him Dione.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.959
However, when her child was born, she was
horrified by his mutation — and upon looking

00:02:15.959 --> 00:02:20.250
into his eyes, she realized he was the harbinger
of the universe's ultimate destruction.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.980
"I've made a huge mistake."

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:27.120
There's a lot more messing up this mother-son
relationship than just unfulfilled expectations

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.430
and a gross chin — Sui-San tried to execute
Thanos as a child, and Thanos successfully

00:02:31.430 --> 00:02:33.180
returned the favor later in life.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.930
Their complex, tumultuous relationship began
with a simple name change.

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.890
"The short-hand is the the butterfly effect.

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:43.100
A butterfly can flap its wings in Peking and
in central park you get rain instead of sunshine."

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.280
Collecting the gems

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:51.269
The Marvel Cinematic Universe spent more than
ten years building up Thanos' search for the

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:54.640
powerful six Infinity Stones — or Gems,
as they used to be known.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:59.120
But it only took him two comic books to accomplish
a goal that's taken a decade to get done on

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:03.920
screen, with the Mad Titan snatching up the
gems one-by-one in a 1990 comic called The

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:04.920
Thanos Quest.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.659
The two-part story saw Thanos travelling the
universe and liberating the six gems from

00:03:08.659 --> 00:03:12.720
their owners, and they were all in very different
hands compared to their cinematic counterparts.

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:17.599
First, Thanos attacked the imprisoned In-Betweener,
stealing the green soul gem from his head.

00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:21.860
Next, he liberated the red power gem from
the Champion in a physical contest, and stole

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:25.440
the time gem from the Gardener, an ageless
Elder of the Universe.

00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:29.160
The yellow reality gem he pilfered from the
Collector, who you may remember from Guardians

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.180
of the Galaxy.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:34.200
The purple space gem was taken from the Runner,
and the blue mind gem was nabbed from the

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:38.730
Grandmaster — yes, that Grandmaster, from
Thor: Ragnarok.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.680
"it's my birthday!

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.629
It's my birthday!"

00:03:42.629 --> 00:03:46.770
All of these foes fell with a surprising quickness
when challenged, clearing the way for Thanos

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:52.550
to assume the powers of a god in the titanic
1991 event series The Infinity Gauntlet.

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.019
Courting Death

00:03:54.019 --> 00:03:58.239
Many of Thanos' stories chronicle the titan's
obsessive passion for the living personification

00:03:58.239 --> 00:03:59.239
of Death.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.740
It's a relationship that was foreshadowed
by his very name.

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:05.970
Jim Starlin originally came up with the character
of Thanos while taking a college psychology

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:06.970
class.

00:04:06.970 --> 00:04:11.120
He based Thanos' personality off of the Freudian
concept of the death drive — in other words,

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.269
the psychological impulse to end one's own
existence.

00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:18.799
His name is reminiscent of Thanatos, the Greek
mythological figure who was said to represent

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:19.799
death.

00:04:19.799 --> 00:04:24.090
In Marvel Comics canon, Death is an actual
person, a skeletal female entity who is sometimes

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:26.660
referred to as Lady or Mistress Death.

00:04:26.660 --> 00:04:31.410
While Thanos is completely in love with her,
Death often refuses to entertain his advances,

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:35.690
or even acknowledge his existence, leading
Thanos to lash out and seek attention through

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.630
his universe-destroying scheme.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.910
While Death does eventually entertain a romance
with Thanos, to say "it's complicated" would

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.180
be putting it lightly.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:45.330
It certainly wasn't worth all of the destruction.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:49.440
In the end, Thanos' battle against the universe's
strongest heroes was all done for the sake

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.720
of impressing a girl.

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:52.990
She's not even all that good-looking.

00:04:52.990 --> 00:04:54.580
My own worst enemy

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:57.640
All of Thanos' bluster covers up a lot of
insecurity.

00:04:57.640 --> 00:05:02.080
As both The Infinity Gauntlet and the characters'
solo outings have shown, Thanos is surprisingly

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:06.600
something of a self-defeating sad-sack.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:09.930
On the surface, his goals would seem to be
the same as any other supervillain: world

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:11.380
domination and destruction.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:14.460
However, Thanos' motivations transcend typical
villainy.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:17.820
He believes in oblivion like a religion, and
all-but-worships Death itself.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:21.070
In his own twisted way, he believes he's doing
the right thing.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:25.669
The universe is unworthy of existence, therefore
it falls on him to give it what it deserves.

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:29.699
The nihilism doesn't stop with his view towards
all other life — it applies to him as well.

00:05:29.699 --> 00:05:31.350
Not even Thanos is worthy.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:35.570
This is why Thanos, despite his power, never
manages to stay on top for too long.

00:05:35.570 --> 00:05:39.740
It's firmly established in Infinity Gauntlet
that he ultimately fails because he allows

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:40.740
himself to.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:45.010
He will always subconsciously leave a hole
in his plans that the heroes can exploit to

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.460
bring about his defeat.

00:05:46.460 --> 00:05:50.470
As much as he believes that the universe deserves
to die, he doesn't believe himself worthy

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:51.710
of the task at hand.

00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:56.220
For such a formidable, otherworldly figure,
that's a pretty human flaw.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:57.720
Thanoseid

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:00.420
Amalgam Comics is a pretty interesting corner
of comics lore.

00:06:00.760 --> 00:06:04.910
A joint venture between Marvel and DC, it
featured characters that were, you guessed

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:07.790
it, amalgamations of Marvel and DC characters.

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:12.160
The world of Amalgam is populated by heroes
like Bruce Wayne: Agent of SHIELD and Doctor

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:14.270
StrangeFate, and it didn't stop with heroes.

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:17.970
The universe also featured amalgamations of
villains from both publishers — and you

00:06:17.970 --> 00:06:20.669
can probably guess who Thanos was paired with.

00:06:20.669 --> 00:06:23.090
Thanos and Darkseid combined to form Thanoseid.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:28.080
Like Darkseid, Thanoseid rules the planet
of Apokalips, and like Thanos, he has an ambition

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:29.590
to wipe out the universe.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.400
In the events that led to their combining
in the Amalgam universe, Darkseid actually

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:38.510
insulted Thanos, calling Thanos just a pale
imitation of him — a funny nod to Thanos'

00:06:38.510 --> 00:06:39.510
origins.

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:43.160
Amalgam's comics weren't exactly classics,
but they were a whole lot of fun.

00:06:43.160 --> 00:06:45.199
Kicking it with the boys

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:49.810
One might reasonably assume the Marvel Universe
only had room for one nihilistic death titan.

00:06:49.810 --> 00:06:50.990
That would be incorrect.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:54.950
One of the more interesting corners of Thanos'
history involves a personal army of clones

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.360
he made of himself.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:07:00.039
These clones are known as the Thanosi, and
are formed by Thanos splicing his DNA with

00:07:00.039 --> 00:07:02.140
that of other Marvel heroes and villains.

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:05.440
There's Omega, a cross between Thanos and
Galactus, for instance.

00:07:05.440 --> 00:07:09.319
Thanos creates the Thanosi to test the abilities
of enemies and allies alike.

00:07:09.319 --> 00:07:12.040
Eventually he considers them failures and
abandons them.

00:07:12.040 --> 00:07:15.600
Shockingly, the Thanosi don't take this betrayal
particularly well.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.530
They band together and, being an army of Thanos
clones, attempt to bring about the ultimate

00:07:19.530 --> 00:07:20.729
end of the universe.

00:07:20.729 --> 00:07:21.760
Luckily, they fail.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:25.650
Given Thanos' general tendencies, an army
of Thanos clones ending up trying to destroy

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:28.440
the universe isn't any kind of surprise.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:30.000
My brother, the lover

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:34.240
No matter how many times he impressively destroys
the universe or allies himself with the good

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:37.639
guys, Thanos will never be as loved as his
brother Starfox.

00:07:37.639 --> 00:07:39.380
No, not that Starfox.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:44.139
The Starfox of the Marvel Universe, also called
Eros, is a carefree, easygoing flirt.

00:07:44.139 --> 00:07:48.160
His charming personality is only amplified
by his superpowers, which include a sort of

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:49.160
pheromone effect.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:53.600
He can make people within 25 feet of him feel
joy, effectively drawing them to him.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:57.910
When cranked up, it can provoke romantic feelings
— he's basically a sentient Marvin Gaye

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:01.889
record, which is pretty tough to compete with
when you're a lumpy, purple death titan.

00:08:01.889 --> 00:08:05.410
Starfox couldn't be any more different from
his brother Thanos, and that's probably a

00:08:05.410 --> 00:08:09.740
good thing — can you imagine if those parents
had to put up with not just one, but two lousy

00:08:09.740 --> 00:08:10.740
kids?

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:11.740
Thanks for watching!

00:08:11.740 --> 00:08:13.360
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:15.240
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

